## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to blend topological ordering with DP to compute the longest-path in a weighted DAG and count the number of critical paths, including multiple sources and modulo arithmetic.

## Key Concepts
- Longest-path in DAG with node durations and edge setup weights
- Topological sort (Kahn) to process in dependency order
- DP for counting number of longest paths with modulo

## Code Example
```javascript
function countCriticalPaths(N, edges, dur) {
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  const incoming = Array.from({length: N}, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(N).fill(0);

  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) {
    incoming[v].push([u, w]);
    indeg[v]++;
  }

  const EFT = dur.slice();
  const count = Array(N).fill(0);
  const q = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
    if (indeg[i] === 0) {
      count[i] = 1;
      q.push(i);
    }
  }

  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    for (const [v, w] of incoming[u]) {
      const newEFT = EFT[u] + w + dur[v];
      if (newEFT > EFT[v]) {
        EFT[v] = newEFT;
        count[v] = count[u];
      } else if (newEFT === EFT[v]) {
        count[v] = (count[v] + count[u]) % MOD;
      }
      indeg[u]--;
      if (indeg[u] === 0) q.push(u);
    }
  }

  let maxEFT = 0, totalCritical = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
    if (EFT[i] > maxEFT) {
      maxEFT = EFT[i];
      totalCritical = count[i];
    } else if (EFT[i] === maxEFT) {
      totalCritical = (totalCritical + count[i]) % MOD;
    }
  }
  return { EFT, maxEFT, criticalPaths: totalCritical };
}
```

## Complexity
- Time: O(N + M) for topological sort and DP
- Space: O(N + M) for adjacency and arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Intersects BFS path counting and graph pruning under constraints; tests meticulous edge-case handling.

## Key Concepts
- BFS for unweighted shortest paths
- Path counting with modulo arithmetic
- Handling blocked nodes and unreachable cases
- Complexity: O(N+M)

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestPaths(n, edges, blocked, s, t) {
  const g = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  for (const [v, u] of edges) if (!blocked[v] && !blocked[u]) g[v].push(u);
  const dist = Array(n).fill(Infinity);
  const ways = Array(n).fill(0);
  if (blocked[s] || blocked[t]) return { dist: -1, ways: 0 };
  dist[s] = 0; ways[s] = 1;
  const q = [s];
  while (q.length) {
    const v = q.shift();
    for (const u of g[v]) {
      if (dist[u] === Infinity) {
        dist[u] = dist[v] + 1; ways[u] = ways[v]; q.push(u);
      } else if (dist[u] === dist[v] + 1) {
        ways[u] = (ways[u] + ways[v]) % 1000000007;
      }
    }
  }
  return { dist: dist[t] === Infinity ? -1 : dist[t], ways: ways[t] };
}
```

